Subject: [PATCH 22/26] [PR] Making XLEN and PHYSICAL ADDRESS WIDTH distinct;
 In this way we can support the different phyisical address width specified by
 rv64 [PR] The PBUS was generated with the same sizes of MBUS. Fixed this to
 make the IP 32-bits wide in both addr and data

---
 config/README.md                           |  3 +-
 config/configs/common/config_system.csv    |  3 +-
 config/scripts/config_xilinx.sh            |  1 +
 config/scripts/configuration.py            |  3 +-
 config/scripts/parse_properties_impl.py    | 55 +++++++++++++++++-----
 config/scripts/parse_properties_wrapper.py |  2 +-
 hw/xilinx/make/config.mk                   |  7 ++-
 hw/xilinx/rtl/mbus_buses.svinc             | 20 ++++----
 hw/xilinx/rtl/pbus_buses.svinc             | 16 +++----
 9 files changed, 75 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

diff --git a/config/README.md b/config/README.md
index f62bd83c..f366346f 100644
--- a/config/README.md
+++ b/config/README.md
@@ -37,7 +37,8 @@ The following table details the supported properties.
 |-|-|-|-|
 | CORE_SELECTOR         | Select target RV core (**only for main_bus**)             | CORE_PICORV32, CORE_CV32E40P, CORE_IBEX, CORE_MICROBLAZEV | None (**mandatory value**)
 | VIO_RESETN_DEFAULT    | Select value for VIO resetn (**only for main_bus**)       | [0,1]                                                     | 1
-| XLEN                  | Defines Bus DATA_WIDTH, ADDRESS_WIDTH and Toolchain version | [32,64]                                                 | 32
+| XLEN                  | Defines Bus DATA_WIDTH, supported cores and Toolchain version             | [32,64]                                                 | 32
+| PHYSICAL_ADDR_WIDTH   | Select the phyisical address width. If XLEN=32 it must equal 32. If XLEN=64, it must be > 32 | (32..64) | 32
 
 ### Bus Configuration
 
diff --git a/config/configs/common/config_system.csv b/config/configs/common/config_system.csv
